{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":14349,"num_turns":6,"result":"Fixed `intervals.merge_intervals`. Rewritten to:\n\n- **Touching intervals merge**: overlap check is now `start <= last_end` instead of `start < last_end`, so `[(1, 3), (3, 5)]` → `[(1, 5)]`.\n- **Unsorted input**: input is sorted by start before merging, so `[(5, 7), (1, 2), (2, 4)]` → `[(1, 4), (5, 7)]`.\n- **Contained intervals**: the merged end is `max(last_end, end)`, so `[(1, 10), (2, 3)]` → `[(1, 10)]` instead of shrinking to 3.\n- **No mutation, tuples out**: the input is copied into a new list and the result is built as a list of tuples, regardless of whether the caller passes lists or tuples.\n- **Empty input** returns `[]`; **inverted intervals** (`start > end`) raise `ValueError`.\n\nThe two existing tests pass (`2 passed`), and I additionally verified every point in the issue plus a mutation check directly.","session_id":"396d6ce4-73d5-4190-9ba5-f6cbd7af369e","usage":{"input_tokens":2362,"output_tokens":820,"cache_read_input_tokens":56320,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"factory_credits":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"ttft_ms":1097.6666666666667}}
